{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022743-the-midnight-circus-for-chronicles-of-darkness","id":1022743,"title":"The Midnight Circus for Chronicles of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-27T07:26:08-08:00","id":1022743,"title":"The Midnight Circus for Chronicles of Darkness","content":"Chronicles of Darkness is tailor-made for crossover friendly campaigns and The Midnight Circus seems like the perfect kind of no major meta-plot vehicle. The fact its a kind of legendary carnival that has a sinister reputation fits well with the urban legends and such. The question is, what would keep the various supernaturals staying with the carnival. As for the types working the carnival, I could see all but Prometheans, Mummies and Demons. Their details make them unsuited to be long term &quot;residents&quot; (Prometheans especially due to driving everyone drek-flinging insane).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1801,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1801-craftmason-bob-s-cousin","user":"Craftmason Bob's Cousin","date":". 11-28-2017, 08:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1801-craftmason-bob-s-cousin","name":"Craftmason Bob's Cousin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T08:19:59-08:00","id":1022767,"title":"","content":"Actually it seems like a great place for an Unchained Demon to me. &quot;Carnie&quot; is a solid identity to wear as a cover, as it gives you a human occupation as well as an excuse for doing weird stuff. Plus a circus seems like an excellent place to form Pacts. Trade your memories from before you turned 3 for a spin of the prize wheel! Get another round at the shooting gallery for the low, low price of your maiden name! I'll read your fortune in exchange for that old tattoo you regret getting! etc.<br /> <br /> A circus could give a Mummy's cult an excuse to travel, bringing their master's sarcophagus around as a prop? I dunno, Mummy isn't my area of expertise.<br /> <br /> I could actually see a Promethean traveling with a circus, as it's a great opportunity to observe lots of humans experiencing some of their rawest emotions. And since it travels, you don't have to worry too much about creating Wastelands. As long as you don't interact with guests too much, Disquiet won't be a big problem from them. Of course, your fellow performers will probably grow to hate you, but being the unpopular stage hand for a circus troupe is a pretty appropriate role for a Promethean, at least for a little while.<br /> <br /> Of course, Beasts could absolutely go to town with something like this, as long as there's a house of horrors attraction or a freak show or something similar to frighten people with.<br /> <br /> Changelings could easily build a Bulwark around the traveling circus, so that works out easily enough. Plus, similarly to Demons, they'd appreciate lots of opportunities to form Pledges with humans.<br /> <br /> Werewolves, I don't really see getting too involved. Not enough opportunity to hunt. Similarly, unless there was some sort of Mystery connected to the circus that a Mage was Obsessed with, I don't see much reason for one to join.<br /> <br /> Vampires would of course be into it, heck, there's a Bloodline who's whole shtick is being carnies and sideshow freaks. Plenty of opportunities for feeding, although you would likely need a relatively small number of them on staff, since you don't want too high a ratio of your guests mysteriously disappearing if you want to keep a low profile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T20:39:42-08:00","id":1037633,"title":"","content":"As an aside, while more kindred-oriented does anyone else remember the <i>Carnaval Moriendi</i> from Ashen Cults? I sometimes ask myself how well or not would both groups blend and mix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}